---
import Reading from "../components/Reading.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";

const langs = profile.languages.map((l) => l.language).join(", ");
---

<Reading
  title="About"
  description={`About ${profile.name} — ${profile.title}`}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
  <h1>{profile.name}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{profile.summary}</p>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <h2>Who I am</h2>
  <p>
    I'm Abdullah Tayyab, also known as <strong>Ellife Dash</strong> — a developer
    and IT operations professional based in {profile.location}. For the past five-plus
    years I've kept critical government infrastructure running at Punjab Police, while
    spending my off-hours building real software for real local problems: clinic
    management, citizen healthcare, and automation tooling.
  </p>
  <p>
    I care less about flashy interfaces and more about software that actually works
    offline, loads fast, and respects the person on the other side of the screen. This
    site is a reflection of that: quiet, readable, and substance-first.
  </p>

  <h2>What I do</h2>
  <p>
    On the operations side, I work across a broad range of internal government systems —
    complaints, FIRs, citizen facilitation, tenant and vehicle monitoring, and
    electronic filing. On the engineering side, I build full-stack applications with the
    MERN stack, desktop apps with Electron, PWAs, and Chrome extensions.
  </p>

  <h2>How I think</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Offline-first.</strong> Networks are unreliable; local software should not fall apart when they are.</li>
    <li><strong>Readable over clever.</strong> Code and writing should be understood by a human six months later.</li>
    <li><strong>Small, sharp tools.</strong> Solve the actual problem, then stop.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <div class="callout">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px">Currently</h3>
    <p class="muted">
      Finishing a BSc in Computer Science (Virtual University of Pakistan) and working
      through CS50 and freeCodeCamp certifications. Always happy to talk about clinic
      systems, government tech, or offline-first architecture.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/connect">Connect with me</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/experience">See my experience</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="aside">
    <div class="aside-block">
      <span class="label">Quick facts</span>
      <ul class="aside-list">
        <li><strong>Role:</strong> {profile.title}</li>
        <li><strong>Based in:</strong> {profile.location}</li>
        <li><strong>Experience:</strong> 5+ yrs IT operations</li>
        <li><strong>Languages:</strong> {langs}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="aside-block">
      <span class="label">Online</span>
      <ul class="aside-list">
        <li><a href={profile.links.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.instagram} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram ↗</a></li>
        <li><a href={profile.links.behance} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Behance ↗</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</Reading>
